@tone foundational
@style pattern
@why-posthoc war-room/wr-9-bites-empirical-or-logical

! conclusion: Treat the War Machine as demonstrated infrastructure and build future work on it, not toward proving that it is real.

  + context: War Room decision WR-18 (2026-05-31). Operator: Joe. The first War Machine outing tested whether the infrastructure could drive real work rather than merely display it.

  + IF:
    A working system has driven a full mission lifecycle on a real queue under its own ranking.

  + HOWEVER:
    Before the first outing, the WB-7/8 arc still left the "is it real" question open: the War Machine might have been a dashboard rather than infrastructure that actually drives work.

  + THEN:
    Record the question as answered and make subsequent work build on the demonstrated War Machine rather than toward another hypothetical version of it.

  + BECAUSE:
    Demonstration changes the status of the claim: the first outing cleared the queue unattended across turns under the War Machine's own ranking while earned-closure discipline remained intact.

    + evidence: M-war-machine-first-outing closed on 2026-05-30 at futon3c commit 24df6fc after four discharges, one honest decomposition, and one honest partial, with zero fake-finishes and zero hard-halts.
